  data: {
    LLM: "As declarer (alone or with a called partner), make your contract: win the agreed number of tricks (e.g. 5 for Question/IsIt/Ladies/Solo, 6 for 6 Trick Solo, 8 for Bull Solo or Solo 2). As defenders, set the declarer by preventing the contract.\n\nAfter the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
    Player: "As declarer (alone or with a called partner), make your contract: win the agreed number of tricks (e.g. 5 for Question/IsIt/Ladies/Solo, 6 for 6 Trick Solo, 8 for Bull Solo or Solo 2). As defenders, set the declarer by preventing the contract.\n\nAfter the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
